```javascript
function minCoins(coins, amount) {
  const dp = new Array(amount + 1).fill(Infinity);
  dp[0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= amount; i++) {
    for (const coin of coins) {
      if (coin <= i && dp[i - coin] + 1 < dp[i]) {
        dp[i] = dp[i - coin] + 1;
      }
    }
  }
  return dp[amount] === Infinity ? -1 : dp[amount];
}
```

Bottom-up DP where `dp[i]` is the fewest coins summing to exactly `i`, seeded with `dp[0] = 0` and everything else at infinity. Each amount tries every coin and keeps the best `dp[i - coin] + 1`, so it handles cases where greedy fails, like coins `[1, 3, 4]` and amount 6, where greedy gives 3 but the answer is 2. Time is O(amount × number of coins), space is O(amount).

